  "introduction": {
    "title": "Intervals: The DNA of Melody",
    "text": "An interval is the distance between two notes. Each interval has its own unique emotional character and sonic quality that affects how your melody feels. Understanding intervals gives you an emotional vocabulary. You can deliberately choose intervals to create specific feelings in your solos.",
    "columns": [
      {
        "title": "What Are Intervals?",
        "text": "Example: C to E (major 3rd) sounds happy, while C to Eb (minor 3rd) sounds sad, even though it's just one semitone difference."
      },
      {
        "title": "Emotional Language",
        "text": "Practical Use: Want tension? Use tritones and minor 2nds. Want resolution? Use octaves and perfect 5ths."
      }
    ]
  },
