  "practiceSection": {
    "title": "Interval Training Exercises",
    "items": [
      "Interval Recognition: Play two notes and identify the interval. Start with perfect 5ths and octaves, gradually add more complex intervals. Develops ear training for melodic construction.",
      "Emotional Interval Exercise: Choose an emotion (sad, happy, tense) and create a melody using only intervals that support that emotion. Connects interval theory to emotional expression.",
      "Melodic Contour Practice: Create melodies using only stepwise motion, then only leaps, then combining both for contrast. Develops control over melodic flow and character."
    ]
